.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_ACERT_PRINT_EX 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_ACERT_print_ex ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_print
.Nd X509_ACERT printing routines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509_acert.h
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_print
.Fa "BIO *bp"
.Fa "X509_ACERT *acert"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_print_ex
.Fa "BIO *bp"
.Fa "X509_ACERT *acert"
.Fa "unsigned long nmflags"
.Fa "unsigned long cflag"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_ACERT_print_ex
prints a human readable version of the attribute certificate
.Fa acert
to BIO
.Fa bp .
.Pp
The following data contained in the attribute certificate is printed in
order:
.Bl -bullet
.It
The header text "Attribute certificate:" and "Data:"
(X509_FLAG_NO_HEADER)
.Pp
The attribute certificate version number as defined by the standard,
followed in parentheses by the value contained in the version field in
hexadecimal notation.
If the version number is not a valid value according to the
specification, only the raw value is printed.
See X509_ACERT_get_version(3) for details.
(X509_FLAG_NO_VERSION)
.Pp
The serial number of the attribute certificate (X509_FLAG_NO_SERIAL)
.Pp
The identity of the holder of the attribute certificate.
If the holder issuer name is present, the first GENERAL_NAME returned by
.Xr X509_ACERT_get0_holder_entityName 3
is printed.
If the holder baseCertificateId is present, the issuer name (printed
with X509_NAME_print_ex) and serial number of the holder's certificate
are displayed.
(X509_FLAG_NO_SUBJECT)
.Pp
The name of the attribute certificate issuer as returned from
.Xr X509_ACERT_get0_issuerName 3
and printed using
.Xr X509_NAME_print_ex 3 .
(X509_FLAG_NO_ISSUER)
.Pp
The period of validity between the times returned from
.Xr X509_ACERT_get0_notBefore 3
and
.Xr X509_ACERT_get0_notAfter 3 .
The values are printed as a generalized times using
.Xr ASN1_GENERALIZEDTIME_print 3 .
(X509_FLAG_NO_VALIDITY)
.Pp
The list of attributes contained in the attribute certificate.
The attribute type is printed with
.Xr i2a_ASN1_OBJECT 3 .
String valued attributes are printed as raw string data.
ASN1 encoded values are printed with
.Xr ASN1_parse_dump 3 .
(X509_FLAG_NO_ATTRIBUTES)
.Pp
All X.509 extensions contained in the attribute certificate.
(X509_FLAG_NO_EXTENSIONS)
.Pp
The signature is printed with
.Xr X509_signature_print 3 .
(X509_FLAG_NO_SIGDUMP)
.Pp
If
.Fa cflag
is specifies as X509_FLAG_COMPAT, all of the above data in the attribute
certificate will be printed.
.Pp
The
.Fa nmflags
flag determines the format used to output all fields printed using
.Xr X509_NAME_print_ex 3 .
See
.Xr X509_NAME_print_ex 3
for details.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_print
is equivalent to calling
.Fn X509_ACERT_print_ex
with the
.Fa nmflags
and
.Em cflags
set to XN_FLAG_COMPAT and X509_FLAG_COMPAT respectively.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_ACERT_print_ex
.Fn X509_ACERT_print
return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr X509_NAME_print_ex 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn X509_ACERT_print
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_print_ex
were added in OpenSSL 3.4.
